<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clydeside</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clydeside is the conurbation along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-clyde">River Clyde</a> in west-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glasgow">Glasgow</a>. In the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries it was one of the world's leading centres of shipbuilding and heavy engineering, and its radical labour movement earned it the name Red Clydeside; the decline of these industries brought heavy unemployment between the wars and after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clydeside.jpg" alt="Clydeside" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Br2387 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Greater_Glasgow.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
